# Elixir Koans - 16 Tasks

```elixir
import ExUnit.Assertions
```

## Tasks can be used for asynchronous computations with results

```elixir
def do_other_stuff do
  :timer.sleep(50)
end

task = Task.async(fn -> 3 * 3 end)
do_other_stuff()
```

```elixir
assert Task.await(task) + 1 == ___
```

## If you don't need a result, use start_link/1

```elixir
{result, _pid} = Task.start_link(fn -> 1 + 1 end)
```

```elixir
assert result == ___
```

## Yield returns nil if the task isn't done yet

```elixir
handle =
  Task.async(fn ->
    :timer.sleep(100)
    3 * 3
  end)
```

```elixir
assert Task.yield(handle, 10) == ___
```

## Tasks can be aborted with shutdown

```elixir
handle =
  Task.async(fn ->
    :timer.sleep(100)
    3 * 3
  end)

%Task{pid: pid} = handle
Task.shutdown(handle)
```

```elixir
assert Process.alive?(pid) == ___
```

## Shutdown will give you an answer if it has it

```elixir
handle = Task.async(fn -> 3 * 3 end)
:timer.sleep(10)
```

```elixir
assert Task.shutdown(handle) == {:ok, ___}
```

## You can yield to multiple tasks at once and extract the results

```elixir
squares =
  [1, 2, 3, 4]
  |> Enum.map(fn number -> Task.async(fn -> number * number end) end)
  |> Task.yield_many(100)
  |> Enum.map(fn {_task, {:ok, result}} -> result end)
```

```elixir
assert squares == ___
```

